Exa Lite is a new search type introduced in Exa 3.0 that is designed for cost-sensitive, real-time, and interactive applications like chat, voice agents, and autocomplete, priced at $4 per 1,000 requests [1][2]. It runs on the same underlying index as Exa Auto but is optimized for lower cost by utilizing less compute across the retrieval stack [1]. Unlike legacy modes such as instant or fast, Lite serves exclusively cached content and rejects requests that include live-fetch or certain advanced search parameters [2]. To implement the Lite search type in your code, you specify it within the search options as demonstrated below:

```javascript
const result = await exa.search("your query here", {
  type: "lite",
  numResults: 5
});
```

Because Lite operates using cached data, it offers a high-performance, cost-effective solution for applications where retrieval speed and budget are prioritized over live data freshness [1][2].
